Usage: lask run [--module PATH] [--output text|json|pretty-json] 
                [--log-format text|json] [--trace-id ID] [--no-color] 
                [--arg-decode text|json|auto] [-h|--help] [--confirm] [FUNCTION]
                [ARGS...]

  Run a function (result is not printed)

Available options:
  --module PATH            Path to the entry module (default: "main.lask")
  --output text|json|pretty-json
                           What stdout is written in: the result of eval, or the
                           report of a command
  --log-format text|json   What stderr is written in: logs and diagnostics, as
                           text or JSON Lines
  --trace-id ID            Trace identifier for this execution
  --no-color               Disable colored output
  --arg-decode text|json|auto
                           How to decode function arguments (default: auto)
  -h,--help                Show the help of FUNCTION, or list the module's
                           functions
  --confirm                Approve the confirmation lask.json asks for

Functions in main.lask:
  build            Builds the site into dist.
  clean            Removes dist.
  internal-helper

